{% if vpnc_net_join_server %}
{{ inventory_hostname }} is the vpnc-net server ({{ vpnc_net_ip }}): ansible-playbook monitoring.yml sets it up.
{% elif vpnc_net_join_laptop %}
{{ inventory_hostname }} ({{ vpnc_net_ip }}) is in vpnc-net.

1. Import {{ vpnc_net_join_conf }} into the AmneziaWG app, then delete the file.
2. For the names in {{ vpnc_net_domain }}, on macOS:
     sudo mkdir -p /etc/resolver && echo 'nameserver {{ vpnc_net_server_ip }}' | sudo tee /etc/resolver/{{ vpnc_net_domain }}
{% else %}
{{ inventory_hostname }} ({{ vpnc_net_ip }}) is in vpnc-net. The join file:

  {{ vpnc_net_join_file }}
  {{ vpnc_net_join_sum.stdout | trim }}
  passphrase: {{ vpnc_net_join_pass.stdout }}

1. Send the file and the passphrase to the machine by different channels.
2. There, as {{ ansible_user | default('the user Ansible will log in as') }} (with sudo):
     bash {{ vpnc_net_join_file | basename }}
   It checks the machine, installs the tunnel and waits for the server.
3. Here: put the links into files/probes/{{ inventory_hostname }}/, then
     ansible-playbook probes.yml --limit {{ inventory_hostname }}
4. Delete the join file everywhere, and this note.
{% endif %}
